  "english": "SEVENTH WEEK OF THE ROMANS [Julian Calendar / Latin Section]\n\nIn February:\n\n1. Saturday, Tone 2 [BK]. Gregory the Theologian.\n2. Sunday, Tone 3 [GCh/GZ]. Third [Sunday]. Canticle [Harts] Tone 6 [GK]: \"Today He who was sacrificed\" (Aysor zenaw). Dismissal [Hambartsi] Tone 5 [GDz/G3]: \"With a terrible voice\" (I dzayn ahegh). For what is placed below, wait one week so that you may look up Transfiguration [Vardavar] in the First Volume.\n3. Monday, Tone 6 [GK]. The Maccabees, Eleazar, and the others. Canticle [Harts] Tone 3 [BDz/B3]: \"With Your saints\" (Ynd sourbs k’o).\n4. Tuesday, Tone 7 [DDz/DCh]. The twelve prophets: Hosea, and the others.\n6. Thursday, Tone 1 [ADz/ADz]. Sophia and her three daughters. Canticle [Harts] Tone 4 [BK]: \"We bless You\" (Orhnemk’ zk’ez).\n8. Saturday, Tone 3 [BDz]. The sons and grandsons of the Enlightener.\n9. Sunday, Tone 4 [BK]. Fourth [Sunday]. Dismissal [Hambartsi] Tone 4 [BK]: \"The Resurrection\" (Yzharout’iwn). Eve of the Fast of Catechumens [Arachavorats].\n10. Monday, Tone 5 [GDz/GZ]. Fast of Catechumens. Canticle of Penitence [Harts apashkharut’ean] Tone 4 [BK]: \"The voice of the youths\" (Mankantsn zdzayn).\n13. Thursday, Tone 8 [DK]. Commemoration of Jonah the Prophet.\n14. Friday, Tone 1 [ADz/AZ]. Fast. Presentation of the Lord [Tyarnndarach].\n\nIn March:\n\n2. Sunday, Tone 8 [DK]. Great Lent Eve [Boun Barekendan]. See also the others according to their order in the First Volume, finding the order of this place.\n\nIn April:\n\n7. Monday, Tone 4 [BK]. Feast of the Annunciation of the Holy Virgin.\n20. Sunday, Tone 1 [ADz/AZ]. Easter: the day of the Resurrection of Christ. See according to the order in the First Volume.\n\nIn January:\n\n6. MONDAY, Tone 2 [AK]. Feast of the Nativity and Epiphany of Christ. The period of non-fasting is thirty-five days.\n14. Tuesday, Tone 2 [AK]. John the Forerunner [Karapet].\n15. Wednesday, Tone 3 [BDz]. Canticle of Penitence [Harts apashkharut’ean] Tone 3 [BDz]: \"Who saved\" (Or apresouts`er).\n16. Thursday, Tone 4 [BK]. Peter the Patriarch, Blaise [Vlas], and the others.\n18. Saturday, Tone 6 [GK]. Anton, and Tryphon, Barsama, and Onuphrius the hermits.\n19. Sunday, Tone 7 [DDz]. First [Sunday]. Dismissal [Hambartsi] Tone 7 [DDz/D3]: \"The Resurrection of the Son of God\" (Yzharout’iwn astouatsordvoyn), to the end.\n20. Monday, Tone 8 [DK]. Theodosius the King, and the Holy Children of Ephesus.\n21. Tuesday, Tone 1 [ADz/AZ]. Cyriacus and Julitta, and Gordius, Polyeuctus, and Grigoris. Canticle [Harts] Tone 1 [ADz]: \"We justify You\" (Yzke’z ardar).\n23. Thursday, Tone 3 [BDz]. Vahan of Goghtn, and Eugenia the Virgin, and the others. Canticle [Harts] Tone 2 [AK]: \"Holy God, the Creator\" (Sourb astouats ararichn).\n25. Saturday, Tone 5 [GDz/GZ]. Athanasius and Cyril, Patriarchs.\n26. Sunday, Tone 6 [GK]. Second [Sunday]. Canticle [Harts] Tone 5 [GDz/G3]: \"Creator of all creatures\" (Ararichd tararatsots). Dismissal [Hambartsi] Tone 6 [GK]: \"A lightning-like vision\" (Tesil p’aylaknadzev).\n27. Monday, Tone 7 [DDz]. Eugenius, Macarius, and the others. Canticle [Harts] Tone 2 [AK]: \"O Most High\" (Or bardzreald).\n28. Tuesday, Tone 8 [DK]. Andrew the General, and his army, and the others.\n30. Thursday, Tone 2 [AK]. Adrianus, and his wife Anatolia, and the others. Canticle [Harts] Tone 3 [BDz/B3]: \"Forgiving\" (Anokhakal).",
